====================================================================================================
0. First principles: what the eye plate does
====================================================================================================
A strand that crosses a joint changes length by (its moment arm about the axis) x (angle).
Eye at (x, y) on the plate in the plane of both axes: palm segment arm about X = y, forearm segment arm
about Y = x. So dL ~ y*flex + x*dev (first order), and the servo travel to cancel it over the range is
  T = (|x|*50 deg + |y|*100 deg) / r_spool = 10.0|x| + 20.0|y| servo deg (x, y in mm)
Pretension: a point-symmetric pair cancels the first order. What is left is second order, and above all
WHERE the line pivots: a pivot a height h above the axis plane adds ~ h*theta^2/2 per strand, the same sign
for flex and ext (common mode). The servo cannot cancel common mode: it only becomes pretension.
Common-mode loop stiffness ~ EA/(L_flex + L_ext) = 11.1 kN / 520 mm = 21 N/mm (soft braid 13). Tolerance +-3.0 N -> +-0.14 mm per loop.
  pivot height 0.00 mm, flex 50: pair common mode +0.017 mm = +0.4 N
  pivot height 0.50 mm, flex 50: pair common mode +0.380 mm = +8.1 N
  pivot height 1.25 mm, flex 50: pair common mode +0.944 mm = +20.2 N

